<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Glory of the Duchy of Carniola</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1689">1689</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Die Ehre deß Hertzogthums Crain</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Glory of the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carniola">Carniola</a> is an encyclopedic description of Carniola by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-weikhard-von-valvasor">Johann Weikhard von Valvasor</a>, published in German at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a> in 1689. Its four volumes, with over 500 engravings, cover the land's geography, history, customs and natural wonders, including the intermittent Lake Cerknica and the olm. It is a founding work of Slovene regional history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/the-glory-of-the-duchy-of-carniola.jpg" alt="The Glory of the Duchy of Carniola" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Maksviktor at Slovenian Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Izvirnik_Slave_vojvodine_Kranjske_iz_leta_1689.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
